course: dictionary
lesson: 8262
title: Riddles and double meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A riddle is a puzzle question that needs clever thinking to answer. Many riddles play with double meanings, where one word can mean two different things. «Riddles play with double meanings: "keys" can open locks, or be the black and white keys of a piano.» The clue is in the word itself, and you have to switch from one meaning to the other to solve it.
explain: When Alice asks the answer to a riddle, the Hatter says he has «not the slightest idea». That means he does not know the answer at all. Riddles often make you stop and think in a new way, so do not give up too quickly.
explain: A riddle can also mean something that is hard to understand, a mystery. People say they "talk in riddles" when they speak in a way that is hard to follow. In one story, hungry animals ask the wise Baboon where everyone has gone, and he only winks and gives them riddles about "spots" and "change".
fact: A riddle is a puzzle question that needs clever thinking to answer.
fact: Many riddles play with double meanings, so you must switch from one meaning of a word to another.
fact: «Riddled with» means full of, as in «a wall riddled with holes».
fact: To «talk in riddles» means to speak in a way that is hard to understand.
fact: Riddles appear in old stories too, such as a sphinx who asks a riddle before letting someone pass.
exercise: What is a riddle? | A kind of soft blanket | A loud song sung at parties | A list of numbers that you add up | *A puzzle question that needs clever thinking to answer
exercise: «The wall was riddled with holes.» What does riddled with mean here? | *Full of | Very tall | Safe to touch | Painted over
exercise: Dad says, «Don't talk in riddles, just tell me.» What does talk in riddles mean? | Sing very loudly | Whisper every word | Read a long book aloud | *Speak in a way that is hard to understand
test: «When Alice asks the answer to the riddle, the Hatter says he has not the slightest idea.» What does the Hatter mean? | He wants Alice to solve it for him | He is asleep under the table | *He does not know the answer at all | He knows the answer and is shouting it
test: Which riddle uses a double meaning? | *«Keys can open locks, or be the black and white keys of a piano» | «The dog ran across the park» | «The sun is hot and the sky is blue» | «Two plus two makes four»
exam: What is the best meaning of a riddle? | A kind of heavy rain | A type of fast running race | *A puzzle question that needs clever thinking to answer | A soft toy that makes a noise
